 r←Initial_UC∆Stash2;msg;stashDir;parms;parms2;res;openProjects;bool
⍝ Creates and opens a project for the sole purpose of testing the stash user commands with no
⍝ argument at all. For that the stash project must be the only one that is "open".\
⍝ Rather than closing whatever the user has open - which is what this function used to do, and
⍝ it never opened them again - `∆OPEN_PROJECTS` is set: from then on `U.GetOpenProjects`
⍝ reports just this one project. Nothing else is disturbed. See `Cleanup_UC∆Stash2`.
 r←1
 ∆StashDir←stashDir←FilesAndDirs.GetTempSubDir''
 {}1 ##.APLGit2.Init stashDir
 stashDir ##.APLGit2.Add''
 msg←'Initial commit'##.APLGit2.Commit stashDir
 'Something went wrong'Assert∧/∨/¨'Initial commit' ' 2 files changed'⍷¨⊂∊msg
 parms←⎕SE.Cider.CreateCreateProjectParms stashDir
 ⎕SE.Cider.CreateProject parms
 parms2←⎕SE.Cider.CreateOpenParms''
 parms2.batch←1
 parms2.folder←stashDir
 res←⎕SE.Cider.OpenProject parms2
 Assert∨/'Project successfully opened and established in'⍷∊res
 openProjects←⎕SE.Cider.ListOpenProjects 0
 bool←(FilesAndDirs.NormalizePath¨openProjects[;2])≡¨⊂FilesAndDirs.NormalizePath stashDir
 'The temporary stash project was not found among the open ones'Assert 1=+/bool
 ∆StashProject←openProjects[⍸bool;]
 {}∆SetOpenProjects ∆StashProject
⍝Done
